  "notes": "\"If ~ is not a creature\" has no negated condition in the vocabulary, so it is a conditional on self-is-type Creature with an EMPTY then and the whole effect in else - the shape parse.ts itself uses for \"sacrifice it unless it escaped\" (parse.ts:481). That keeps the guard real: a second activation while it is already a creature does nothing, so the granted trigger is never stacked twice. become adds Creature to the land types (CR 205.1b), so \"It is still a land\" needs nothing extra, and gain-ability puts the quoted trigger on the source itself.",
